<doc-number>1992005203</doc-number><kind>A1</kind></document-id><sources><source category="A" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1026176A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURAMOTO MASAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO HARUHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IDEMITSU PETROCHEMICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAMOTO, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, HARUHITO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KURAMOTO MASAHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO HARUHITO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KURAMOTO, MASAHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, HARUHITO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A highly active catalyst for olefin polymerization; a process for efficiently producing the catalyst; and a process for efficiently producing a high-quality polyolefin reduced in residual metal content using the catalyst and without using a large quantity of an organoaluminum compound. The olefin polymer production process is characterized by using as a catalyst component either a reaction product obtained through contacting from a clay, clay mineral, or ion-exchanging lamellar compound, an organosilane compound, and (C) water or a clay treated with a silane compound.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un catalyseur fortement actif pour une polymérisation oléfinique, ainsi qu'un procédé de production efficace de ce catalyseur. Cette invention concerne également un procédé de production efficace d'une polyoléfine haute qualité présentant une faible teneur en métal résiduel, ce procédé utilisant le catalyseur susmentionné sans avoir recours à une grande quantité d'un composé d'aluminium organique. Ce procédé de production d'un polymère oléfinique se caractérise notamment par l'utilisation, comme composant catalyseur, soit d'un produit de la réaction due à la mise en contact d'un minéral argileux provenant d'une argile, soit d'un composé laminaire échangeur d'ions, d'un composé organosilane, et (C) de l'eau ou une argile traitée avec un composé au silane.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>